# The AUR holds build scripts only, so this hides everything and lets back what a push
# carries. What it keeps out of `git status` — and out of an accidental `git add -A` — is the
# build's whole output: `*.pkg.tar.zst` beside the PKGBUILD, the split `-debug` package, the
# logs `pkgctl build` and `namcap` write, `src/`, `pkg/` and the `SRCDEST` tarball.
*
!.gitignore
!.SRCINFO
!PKGBUILD
!*.install
!*.patch
!LICENSE
!LICENSES
!LICENSES/*
!REUSE.toml
# `pkgctl version setup` writes it and `REUSE.toml` annotates it, so it is a file this
# repository is meant to carry.
!.nvchecker.toml
